{"title":"Why plants need sunlight to make food","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight as energy to turn water and carbon dioxide into food and oxygen through photosynthesis.","method":["Identify the three raw materials a plant needs: sunlight, water from soil, and carbon dioxide from air.","Understand that sunlight acts as the energy source, like electricity powering a factory.","Recognize that the plant uses this energy to combine water and carbon dioxide and create food for itself and oxygen as a waste product.","Remember that without sunlight, the plant cannot make food and will weaken over time."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant is placed indoors on a sunny windowsill for two weeks, then moved to a dark cupboard for two weeks. What will change?","steps":["In sunlight, the plant receives energy to make food from water and carbon dioxide.","The plant grows strong and releases oxygen.","In darkness, the plant cannot make food because there is no energy source.","The plant becomes weak, pale, and may stop growing because it has no food."],"answer":"The plant will weaken and stop growing in darkness because photosynthesis cannot happen without sunlight."},"key_terms":[{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the process where plants make their own food using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide"},{"term":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"a gas in the air that plants take in through tiny holes in their leaves"},{"term":"raw materials","meaning":"the things a plant needs to start with: sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking a plant can make food in darkness if it has water and air—it cannot, because sunlight provides the energy needed.","Forgetting that the plant needs all three things at the same time: if one is missing, photosynthesis stops."],"remember":"Sunlight is the power source; water and air are the materials; food and oxygen are what the plant produces.","quick_check":[{"q":"Why does a plant kept in a dark room become weak even if you water it?","a":"Because it cannot make food without sunlight, and food gives the plant energy to grow."},{"q":"What gas does a plant release during photosynthesis?","a":"Oxygen."}],"tell_your_child":"Think of your plant as a solar-powered factory: it needs sunlight like a solar panel needs sun to work. Without the sun's energy, even with water and air, the factory cannot turn those materials into food, so the plant gets tired and weak."}
```
